# Hebrew/RTL Support

## Summary

This document provides detailed patterns for implementing Hebrew and Right-to-Left (RTL) support in form components, dialogs, and navigation elements. It covers:

- **Critical Requirements**: Always implementing RTL support for forms, dialogs, and navigation
- **TextField Hebrew Support**: Using `data-hebrew` prop and RTL-aware styling
- **Autocomplete RTL Support**: Complete implementation with `data-hebrew` and `data-rtl` props, endAdornment positioning, and renderOption RTL handling
- **Direction and Alignment**: Setting `dir` prop and text alignment based on language
- **Theme Variants**: Using Hebrew typography variants from theme
- **Progress Bar (LinearProgress)**: Container direction, label alignment, and bar fill direction (scaleX) for RTL
- **Component Patterns**: TextField, Autocomplete, Select, and other form components with full RTL support

This is a specialized guide for form components. For comprehensive RTL layout patterns, see [Hebrew Language & RTL Support](./hebrew-support.mdc).

## 🇮🇱 Hebrew/RTL Support

### ⚠️ Critical Requirement

**ALWAYS implement Hebrew/RTL support for all form components, dialogs, and navigation elements:**

- ✅ **TextField**: Use `data-hebrew` prop when `i18n.language === "he"`
- ✅ **Autocomplete**: Use both `data-hebrew` and `data-rtl` props for Hebrew
- ✅ **Direction**: Always set `dir` prop to `"rtl"` or `"ltr"` based on language
- ✅ **Text Alignment**: Use `textAlign` with RTL condition
- ✅ **Theme Variants**: Use Hebrew typography variants from `app/theme.ts` when appropriate

### TextField Hebrew Support

**ALWAYS use `data-hebrew` prop for TextField components in Hebrew:**

```typescript
import { TextField } from "@mui/material";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";

const { i18n } = useTranslation();

<TextField
    label={t("fields.first_name")}
    value={value}
    onChange={(e) => handleChange(e.target.value)}
    {...(i18n.language === "he" && { "data-hebrew": true })}
    dir={i18n.language === "he" ? "rtl" : "ltr"}
/>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Use `data-hebrew={true}` when `i18n.language === "he"`
- ✅ Always set `dir` prop: `dir={i18n.language === "he" ? "rtl" : "ltr"}`
- ✅ Theme automatically handles RTL label positioning, text alignment, and outline direction
- ✅ Works with all TextField variants (outlined, filled, standard)
- ✅ Supports multiline TextFields (theme has specific variant for this)

**Reference:** See `app/theme.ts` lines 662-777 for `data-hebrew` variant styling.

### Autocomplete Hebrew Support

**ALWAYS use both `data-hebrew` and `data-rtl` props for Autocomplete components:**

```typescript
import { Autocomplete, TextField } from "@mui/material";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";

const { i18n } = useTranslation();
const isHebrew = i18n.language === "he";

<Autocomplete
    options={options}
    value={value}
    onChange={(_, newValue) => handleChange(newValue)}
    getOptionLabel={(option) => option.label}
    dir={isHebrew ? "rtl" : "ltr"}
    {...(isHebrew && {
        "data-hebrew": true,
        "data-rtl": true,
    })}
    sx={{
        "& .MuiAutocomplete-endAdornment": {
            right: isHebrew ? "auto" : "9px",
            left: isHebrew ? "9px" : "auto",
        },
    }}
    renderInput={(params) => (
        <TextField
            {...params}
            label={t("fields.business_unit")}
            {...(isHebrew && { "data-hebrew": true })}
            dir={isHebrew ? "rtl" : "ltr"}
        />
    )}
    renderOption={(props, option) => {
        const { key, ...otherProps } = props;
        return (
            <li
                key={key}
                {...otherProps}
                style={{
                    direction: isHebrew ? "rtl" : "ltr",
                    textAlign: isHebrew ? "right" : "left",
                    paddingRight: isHebrew ? "16px" : "14px",
                    paddingLeft: isHebrew ? "14px" : "16px",
                }}
            >
                <Typography
                    sx={{
                        direction: isHebrew ? "rtl" : "ltr",
                        textAlign: isHebrew ? "right" : "left",
                        width: "100%",
                    }}
                >
                    {option.label}
                </Typography>
            </li>
        );
    }}
/>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Use both `data-hebrew` and `data-rtl` props on Autocomplete root
- ✅ Use `data-hebrew` prop on TextField inside `renderInput`
- ✅ Always set `dir` prop on both Autocomplete and TextField
- ✅ Override `endAdornment` positioning in `sx` prop (left/right swap)
- ✅ **CRITICAL**: Always style `renderOption` with RTL-aware inline styles
- ✅ Use RTL-aware padding in `renderOption` (swap left/right)
- ✅ Wrap option content in Typography with RTL direction

**Reference:** See `app/theme.ts` lines 929-986 for `data-rtl` variant styling.

### Breadcrumbs RTL Support

**ALWAYS implement RTL support for Breadcrumbs:**

```typescript
import { Breadcrumbs, Link, Typography } from "@mui/material";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";

const { i18n } = useTranslation();
const isHebrew = i18n.language === "he";

<Breadcrumbs
    sx={{
        mb: 2,
        width: "100%",
        direction: isHebrew ? "rtl" : "ltr",
        "& .MuiBreadcrumbs-ol": {
            flexWrap: "nowrap",
            overflow: "hidden",
            width: "100%",
            display: "flex",
            alignItems: "center",
            flexDirection: isHebrew ? "row-reverse" : "row",
            justifyContent: isHebrew ? "flex-end" : "flex-start",
        },
        "& .MuiBreadcrumbs-separator": {
            marginLeft: isHebrew ? 0 : theme.spacing(0.5),
            marginRight: isHebrew ? theme.spacing(0.5) : theme.spacing(0.5),
        },
    }}
>
    {(() => {
        const breadcrumbItems = [
            <Link key="parent" component="button" onClick={() => router.back()}>
                {t("sections.parent")}
            </Link>,
            <Typography key="current" color="text.primary">
                {currentPage}
            </Typography>,
        ];
        // Reverse items for Hebrew
        return isHebrew ? breadcrumbItems.slice().reverse() : breadcrumbItems;
    })()}
</Breadcrumbs>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Set `direction` on Breadcrumbs root
- ✅ Use `flexDirection: "row-reverse"` for Hebrew
- ✅ Swap `justifyContent` (flex-end for Hebrew, flex-start for English)
- ✅ Adjust separator margins (swap left/right)
- ✅ **CRITICAL**: Reverse breadcrumb items array for Hebrew: `isHebrew ? items.slice().reverse() : items`
- ✅ Apply RTL direction and textAlign to each Link/Typography item

### Button Icon Spacing RTL Support

**ALWAYS handle icon spacing for buttons in RTL:**

```typescript
import { Button, CircularProgress } from "@mui/material";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";

const { i18n } = useTranslation();
const isRTL = i18n.language === "he";

<Button
    variant="contained"
    disabled={isLoading}
    endIcon={isLoading ? (
        <CircularProgress size={16} sx={{ color: "inherit" }} />
    ) : undefined}
    sx={{
        direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
        "& .MuiButton-endIcon": {
            marginLeft: isRTL ? 0 : theme.spacing(1),
            marginRight: isRTL ? theme.spacing(1) : 0,
        },
        "& .MuiButton-startIcon": {
            marginRight: isRTL ? 0 : theme.spacing(1),
            marginLeft: isRTL ? theme.spacing(1) : 0,
        },
    }}
>
    {t("actions.save", { ns: "common" })}
</Button>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Set `direction` on Button `sx` prop
- ✅ Swap `marginLeft` and `marginRight` for `endIcon` in RTL
- ✅ Swap `marginRight` and `marginLeft` for `startIcon` in RTL
- ✅ Use `startIcon` for Hebrew, `endIcon` for English (when appropriate)

### Switch Component RTL Support

**ALWAYS use `data-rtl` prop for Switch components in Hebrew:**

```typescript
import { Switch, FormControlLabel } from "@mui/material";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";

const { i18n } = useTranslation();
const isHebrew = i18n.language === "he";

<FormControlLabel
    control={
        <Switch
            checked={checked}
            onChange={(e) => handleChange(e.target.checked)}
            color="primary"
            {...(isHebrew && { "data-rtl": true })}
        />
    }
    label={t("fields.status")}
/>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Use `data-rtl={true}` when `i18n.language === "he"`
- ✅ Theme automatically handles RTL transform (`scaleX(-1)`)
- ✅ Works with both regular and small size switches

**Reference:** See `app/theme.ts` lines 1966-2015 for `data-rtl` Switch variant styling.

### Progress Bar (LinearProgress) RTL Support

**ALWAYS implement RTL support for progress indicators (e.g. upload progress) that include a label and LinearProgress:**

```typescript
import { Box, LinearProgress, Paper, Typography, CircularProgress } from "@mui/material";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";

const { t, i18n } = useTranslation(["common"]);
const isRTL = i18n.language === "he";

<Paper
    sx={{
        p: theme.spacing(2),
        direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
        textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left",
        // ... other styles
    }}
>
    <Box
        sx={{
            display: "flex",
            alignItems: "center",
            flexDirection: isRTL ? "row-reverse" : "row",
            gap: theme.spacing(1),
            mb: theme.spacing(1),
        }}
    >
        <CircularProgress size={16} color="primary" />
        <Typography
            variant="body2"
            sx={{
                flex: 1,
                minWidth: 0,
                direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
                textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left",
            }}
        >
            {t("messages.uploading")}
        </Typography>
    </Box>
    <Box sx={{ direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr" }}>
        <LinearProgress
            sx={{
                height: 6,
                borderRadius: 3,
                ...(isRTL && { transform: "scaleX(-1)" }),
                // ... other styles
            }}
        />
    </Box>
</Paper>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Set `direction` and `textAlign` on the progress container (e.g. Paper) so the block flows RTL
- ✅ Use `flexDirection: isRTL ? "row-reverse" : "row"` on the row that contains icon + label so the icon appears on the right in Hebrew
- ✅ Give the label `flex: 1` and `minWidth: 0` so it takes remaining space; set `textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left"` so the label text aligns to the right in Hebrew
- ✅ **Bar fill direction**: In RTL, apply `transform: "scaleX(-1)"` to `LinearProgress` so the bar fills from right to left (progress toward the left)
- ✅ Wrap `LinearProgress` in a `Box` with `direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr"` so the flipped bar aligns correctly within the layout

**Reference:** See `shared/layout-components/activity/ActivityFileUploader.tsx` for upload progress with LinearProgress RTL.

### RadioButton and RadioGroup RTL Support

**ALWAYS implement RTL support for RadioGroup and FormControlLabel components:**

```typescript
import { RadioGroup, FormControlLabel, Radio, Box, Typography } from "@mui/material";
import { Person as PersonIcon, Group as GroupIcon } from "@mui/icons-material";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";

const { i18n } = useTranslation();
const isRTL = i18n.language === "he";

// Container Box for alignment
<Box sx={{ 
    display: "flex",
    flexDirection: "column",
    alignItems: isRTL ? "flex-end" : "flex-start",
    direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
}}>
    <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ 
        mb: 1,
        textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left",
        direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
        width: "100%",
    }}>
        {t("sections.share_with")}
    </Typography>
    
    <RadioGroup
        row={true}
        value={value}
        onChange={(e) => handleChange(e.target.value)}
        sx={{
            direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
            flexDirection: isRTL ? "row-reverse" : "row",
            gap: 2,
            justifyContent: isRTL ? "flex-end" : "flex-start",
            width: "100%",
        }}
    >
        <FormControlLabel
            value="option1"
            control={<Radio />}
            label={
                <Box sx={{ 
                    display: "flex", 
                    alignItems: "center", 
                    gap: 0.5,
                    direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
                    flexDirection: "row",
                }}>
                    {isRTL ? (
                        <>
                            <Icon fontSize="small" />
                            <Typography sx={{
                                direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
                                textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left",
                            }}>{t("fields.option1")}</Typography>
                        </>
                    ) : (
                        <>
                            <Icon fontSize="small" />
                            <Typography sx={{
                                direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
                                textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left",
                            }}>{t("fields.option1")}</Typography>
                        </>
                    )}
                </Box>
            }
            sx={{
                direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
                justifyContent: isRTL ? "flex-end" : "flex-start",
                "& .MuiFormControlLabel-label": {
                    marginLeft: isRTL ? 0 : theme.spacing(1),
                    marginRight: isRTL ? theme.spacing(1) : 0,
                },
            }}
        />
    </RadioGroup>
</Box>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ **Container Box**: Use `alignItems: isRTL ? "flex-end" : "flex-start"` to align RadioGroup to the right for Hebrew
- ✅ **RadioGroup**: Always use `row={true}` (not conditional)
- ✅ **RadioGroup sx**: Set `direction`, `flexDirection: isRTL ? "row-reverse" : "row"`, and `justifyContent: isRTL ? "flex-end" : "flex-start"`
- ✅ **FormControlLabel sx**: Set `direction`, `justifyContent: isRTL ? "flex-end" : "flex-start"` to position radio button on the right for Hebrew
- ✅ **Label margins**: Swap `marginLeft` and `marginRight` for `.MuiFormControlLabel-label` in RTL
- ✅ **Label content**: For labels with icons, place icon first in DOM for RTL to appear on the right side of text
- ✅ **Typography in label**: Always set `direction` and `textAlign` for Typography within labels
- ✅ **Label Box**: Set `direction` and `flexDirection: "row"` (not reversed) for proper icon/text positioning

**Icon Positioning in Labels:**
- For Hebrew (RTL): Icon first in DOM order, then Typography (icon appears on right of text)
- For LTR: Icon first in DOM order, then Typography (icon appears on left of text)
- Use conditional rendering if icon order needs to differ between RTL/LTR

**Reference:** See `components/reports/ShareReportModal.tsx` for complete RadioGroup RTL implementation.

